A||||3||HummelHund||84' SE Problems||||1||
Z||000000||HummelHund||07-18-2001||02:31 PM||||Though, with the help of this forum, I have fixed most of what's wrong with my 84' SE, it still has a couple of nagging problems. The first is rough/high idle while it's warming up. It will first idle low and rough, then rev up to 1500-2000 rpm by itself (should I call an exorcist?). After about 2-3 minutes the idle stabilizes at a normal 900 rpm. I've replaced the MAP, TPS, and IAC, and most of the vacuum lines. I cannot find any leaks in any of the lines. The one thing that I can see is the electrical connector to the MAP is frayed (the green wire). Could this cause it? Is there anythign else I should replace? The other problem I'm having is a battery drain that I cannot find. What are the most common reasons for battery drains on 84' 4 cylinders? It's a new battery. <BR>Thanks in advance for any help.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||07-18-2001||05:31 PM||||I am not sure about your motor problems.but your battery drainage problem should be easy to figure out.if you have a volt meter or ifnot a test light will work disconnect the positive cable from the battery then connect one of the leads from your meter or test lightto the cable the other lead to the battery.you will pull fuses 1 @ a time till you have no current passing thru the leads this is a very abreviated instruction of what you need to do diagnos your battery  problem.If you need more detailed instructions I or some one else here on the forum will be happy to do so .hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000002||HummelHund||07-18-2001||09:18 PM||||Thanks, I'll try that. Doesn't sound too hard.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||07-18-2001||11:25 PM||||I think this was posted before,<P>My fiero, 84 2m4, and a lot of other peoples have the same experience with the high idle warm up.  I think that all the early 2m4s did it and you cant do anything to fix it.<P>If its really bad, you can try changing the coolent temp sensor.  If yours is the original, you will have to crimp on a new plug which is included in the box when you buy it.||||reg||1
